WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.998
Custom furniture sounds like the best fit.

00:00:05.278 --> 00:00:06.833
But is it really what you need?

00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:11.334
Fully custom units take longer to design and make, cost more,

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:16.258
and can be hard to extend or repair later, because nothing else matches them.

00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:20.252
Custom pieces also make every new station a new project.

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:27.357
A configured solution builds your exact station from standard, proven modules across one system:

00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:31.151
the right bench, worktop, storage, size and accessories.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:37.222
You still get a station tailored to your process, but it is quicker to deliver, more economical,

00:00:37.222 --> 00:00:39.937
and easy to extend with matching parts later.

00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:44.313
And if something wears out years later, matching spares are still available.

00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:49.013
One clean-tech manufacturer asked for custom tables,

00:00:49.013 --> 00:00:55.637
then chose standard Furnisys 72 by 36 by 30 inch workstations for faster deployment.

00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:59.843
Truly custom sizes remain possible, with a longer lead time.

00:01:00.443 --> 00:01:04.629
Start with configuration, and customise only what is truly unique.

00:01:04.909 --> 00:01:06.793
What part of your setup feels custom?

00:01:07.073 --> 00:01:11.464
Comment below, and next, see how warranty and after-sales support work.

00:01:12.064 --> 00:01:16.309
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

